{
  "eyebrow": "Morning Brief",
  "headline": "Payrolls 8:30 consensus 84K, ISM 54.5 vs 55.0, 10y high 5.34% Thursday, OAT-Bund 2012 wide",
  "stance": "Payrolls at 8:30 lands on a long end that reversed a 2002 high Thursday. France, not the US, drove overnight risk.",
  "news": [
    {
      "head": "France sent its 2027 budget to parliament",
      "body": "€54bn of cuts, deficit target 5% of GDP from 5.4% this year. OAT-Bund is at its widest since 2012."
    },
    {
      "head": "Hang Seng fell 2.6% Friday",
      "body": "Its first session after the Oct 1 holiday. European shares are set for their worst week since April."
    },
    {
      "head": "ISM Manufacturing missed at 54.5",
      "body": "Against 55.0 expected and 54.6 in August. Expansion, but slower than August."
    },
    {
      "head": "Crude rose Thursday on the Iran export blockade",
      "body": "OVX is above 51. Rate markets have not priced an energy-led inflation leg."
    }
  ],
  "implications": [
    "Payrolls moves the front end; France moves the long end. Two drivers, and only one of them trades at 8:30.",
    "A hot payroll number pushes the dollar into extended-short sterling and euro positions. The squeeze would be in FX, not rates."
  ],
  "watch": [
    {
      "head": "Jobs report, 8:30",
      "body": "Consensus 84K after 162K in August. Unemployment seen 4.1%, average hourly earnings +0.3%."
    },
    {
      "head": "Factory orders, 10:00",
      "body": "August shipments, inventories and orders. It matters only if the 8:30 number is quiet."
    },
    {
      "head": "French budget now goes to the Assembly",
      "body": "A minority government needs the votes. OAT-Bund is where it shows."
    },
    {
      "head": "CPI, Oct 14",
      "body": "The last inflation read before the next Fed decision."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Macro & Rates",
      "bullets": [
        "The 10y traded 5.34% Thursday, a 2002 high, and closed 10bp below it. No US release did that.",
        "September added over 50bp to the 10y, its biggest monthly rise since 2022. October starts from that level.",
        "Payrolls at 8:30 is a front-end event. Europe sets the long end now, and that does not clear today."
      ],
      "positioning": "COT, Sep 22: sterling specs fell to the 2nd percentile of 3 years, down 20 points on the week.",
      "single_name": null
    },
    {
      "title": "Equity Markets",
      "bullets": [
        "S&P breadth improved to 24.7% above the 50-day Thursday, from 21.9% Wednesday. Narrow, but no longer narrowing.",
        "Front-month vol carries no payroll premium. The tail sits in SKEW instead, and that is a different trade.",
        "S&P futures +0.5%, Nasdaq-100 +0.8% pre-market (~6am ET). Europe is lower at the same hour."
      ],
      "positioning": "COT, Sep 22: Nasdaq 100 specs reached the 100th percentile of 3 years, up 25 points on the week.",
      "single_name": null
    },
    {
      "title": "Credit & Liquidity",
      "bullets": [
